
==============================================================================
[A] exact Haar reference, a0 = (1/2)tr U = cos(phi/2), phi = 2 arccos a0 in [0,2pi)
==============================================================================
  quadrature 4000 pt GL:  E[phi]   = 3.141592654   (closed form pi = 3.141592654)
                         E[phi^2] = 11.159472535   (4pi^2/3 - 2 = 11.159472535)
                         Var(phi) = 1.289868134   (pi^2/3 - 2   = 1.289868134)
                         (1/3)E[phi^2] = 3.719824178   ((4pi^2-6)/9 = 3.719824178)
                         E[a0] = +2.78e-17, Var(a0) = 0.250000000 (=1/4), E[a0^4] = 0.125000000 (=1/8)
                         P(|a0|>0.9) = 0.037290   (closed form 0.037386)
  => THE IDENTITY: 3.719824 = (1/3)E[(2 arccos a0)^2] = (1/3)E[|xi|^2], NOT Var(2 arccos a0).
     Var(2 arccos a0)|Haar = pi^2/3 - 2 = 1.289868134, because E[2 arccos a0] = pi.
     So the two differ by the mean square of the mean: 1.289868 + pi^2 = 11.159473 = 3 x 3.719824.

